      </TextBlock>
      <TextBlock layer="Layer 1" zorder="-2">
        <Transform ScaleX="2118.0" ScaleY="240.0" ShearX="0.0" ShearY="0.0" TranslateX="68.06761805037937" TranslateY="24.04856158265771"/>
        <Content>
          <span family="Arial" size="32.0" bold="true">Simplified Models for Electrolysers 
</span>
          <span family="Arial" size="28.0">The simplified models for electrolysers allow the user to simulate different types of electrolysers such as Alkaline electrolysers (AEL), Anion Exchange Membrane (AEM) electrolysers, Proton Exchange Membrane (PEM) electrolysers, and Solid Oxide electrolysers (SOE). These models offer the capability to model electrolysers either on a constant efficiency basis or through performance curves. The latter includes overall performance curves and polarisation curves for both multiple and single stack configurations.</span>
        </Content>
        <Border style="NO_BORDER" width="1">
          <lineColour Red="0" Green="0" Blue="0"/>
          <shadowColour Red="0" Green="0" Blue="0"/>
        </Border>
      </TextBlock>
